# Force LF for all text so committed bytes are stable across OSes. This is
# REQUIRED for the served data files: the data manifest records each file's
# SHA-256 of its exact bytes, and the loader verifies that hash before use
# (P-01/P-02). A CRLF checkout would change the bytes and break verification.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source inputs are committed BYTE-FOR-BYTE (coordinator's explicit say-so) and
# never edited or normalised. `-text` stops any EOL conversion so the stored
# bytes equal the originals exactly. (The SERVED data in public/data/ is still
# LF-normalised by the rule above — that is what the loader hashes.)
data/source/** -text

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
